# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# iPhone app — build-time configuration
#
# For local development: copy to mobile/.env (git-ignored) and fill in. The development
# server reads it and compiles the values into the JavaScript it serves to the development
# build on your iPhone.
# For EAS cloud builds: .env files are not uploaded. Values go in eas.json instead:
#   - EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID → build.base.env (same for every build)
#   - EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL → build.preview.env / build.production.env, and only once you
#     have a deployed https URL. Never leave a key empty in eas.json — EAS rejects it; omit
#     the key instead.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_* values are compiled into the app binary. They are NOT secrets and
# must never be: no API keys, no client secrets, no tokens belong here.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Google Cloud → Credentials → OAuth client ID → type **iOS** → bundle ID = APP_BUNDLE_ID.
# Looks like 1234567890-abc123def456.apps.googleusercontent.com
# The app derives its OAuth redirect (com.googleusercontent.apps.1234567890-abc123def456:/oauth2redirect)
# and registers it as a URL scheme automatically.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID=

# Base URL of the server's /api/v1 (rules-pack updates + the optional AI fallback proxy).
# Optional: without it the app uses the rules pack bundled in the build and the AI fallback
# stays unavailable. Gmail sync, parsing and everything else work without it.
#   Development (this file): http://<your Mac's Wi-Fi IP>:4000 — find it with
#                `ipconfig getifaddr en0`. Never "localhost": on the iPhone that means the
#                phone itself. The phone must be on the same Wi-Fi as the Mac.
#   Preview / production (eas.json): the https URL of your deployed server, e.g. the
#                Render URL from SETUP.md Part 8.2. A Mac's LAN address does not belong in a
#                cloud build — it only works on your home network and changes over time.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=

# Optional. Only if the server sets LLM_PROXY_SHARED_TOKEN. Ships inside the app, so it is an
# abuse deterrent for the proxy, not a secret.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_APP_TOKEN=

# Local Xcode builds with a free Apple Personal Team (PERSONAL_IPHONE.md). Optional, not secrets.
#   APPLE_TEAM_ID — your 10-character team ID; kept in the generated Xcode project so signing
#                   survives `npm run ios:prebuild`. Leave unset to choose the team in Xcode.
#   IOS_DATA_PROTECTION_ENTITLEMENT=1 — adds the Data Protection entitlement. Off by default so
#                   free Personal Team signing always works.
# APPLE_TEAM_ID=
# IOS_DATA_PROTECTION_ENTITLEMENT=

# Optional overrides read by app.config.ts (you can also edit the defaults there).
# APP_BUNDLE_ID=com.yourname.expensetracker
# APP_DISPLAY_NAME=Expense Tracker
# EAS_PROJECT_ID=
